    "questionDiagrams": [],
    "children": [],
    "answer": {
      "short": "No. A set can have multiple valid representations.",
      "worked": "No. For example, $\\{1,2,3\\}=\\{3,2,1\\}$; both also describe the positive integers less than $4$. The elements determine the set, not the form of its representation.",
